      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

      <p>
        This Privacy Policy describes how Yacht Evaluator for Clubhouse Games (hereinafter referred to as "the Service") handles user information.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>The Service may collect the following information:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Access Log Information</strong>: Information automatically recorded by the server, such as IP addresses, browser types, access times, and referrer information
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Gameplay Data</strong>: Game state information entered when using the Service, such as dice values, score sheets, and roll counts
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Purpose of Use</h2>
      <p>The collected information is used for the following purposes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>To provide and operate the Service</li>
        <li>To provide game situation evaluation and analysis features</li>
        <li>To improve and develop the Service</li>
        <li>To prevent unauthorized use and maintain security</li>
        <li>To respond to inquiries</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Protection of Personal Information</h2>
      <p>
        The Service does not actively collect personally identifiable information (such as names, email addresses, or physical addresses). Gameplay data is processed temporarily only to the extent necessary for evaluation features and is not used to identify individuals.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Disclosure to Third Parties</h2>
      <p>
        The Service will not provide personal information to third parties without user consent, except as required by law.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
      <p>
        The Service may use browser local storage to temporarily save game state for improved user convenience. This information is managed only within the user's browser and is not transmitted externally.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Use of External Services</h2>
      <p>
        The Service may use the following external services for access analysis and service improvement. These services collect and use information according to their own privacy policies.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Google Analytics (for access analysis)</li>
        <li>Other external API services necessary for service operation</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Please refer to each service provider's website for their privacy policies.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Children's Personal Information</h2>
      <p>
        The Service does not intentionally collect personal information from children under 13 years of age. Parents and guardians are requested to provide appropriate supervision when children use the Service.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes to Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy may be changed without notice in response to legal revisions or changes in service content. The revised Privacy Policy will take effect when posted on this page.
      </p>

